ProsperoSunshine: a session's description names the packet size it asked for

The host keeps the last streams that ended (control/stream_history.hpp, for the web page) and says of each whether the
device came over the internet, which is one that asks for Moonlight's small packets (prospero::remote_packet_size). The
size is set before the session is listed and never changes, as the rest of what describe() reads from the config.

--- a/src/rtsp.h
+++ b/src/rtsp.h
@@ -163,6 +163,7 @@
     std::uint32_t recoveries = 0;  ///< Times the client asked for an IDR or to invalidate reference frames.
     std::uint32_t rtt_ms = 0;  ///< Round-trip time of the control connection, 0 until known.
     std::uint32_t missing_frames = 0;  ///< Frames the client reported lost (the ranges it asked to invalidate).
+    int packet_size = 0;  ///< Packet size the client asked for; Moonlight asks for a small one over the internet.
   };
 
   /**
--- a/src/stream.cpp
+++ b/src/stream.cpp
@@ -2392,6 +2392,7 @@
       result.recoveries = session.info_recoveries.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
       result.rtt_ms = session.info_rtt_ms.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
       result.missing_frames = session.info_missing_frames.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+      result.packet_size = session.config.packetsize;
       return result;
     }
 
